With this, `<script type="application/ld+json" src="./schema.json"></script>` doesn't work, but as far as I understand, this isn't how these schemas are used?

The HTMLPackager only replaces its own hashes with urls, but not inside inline bundles.
You need to create a new packager (`@parcel/packager-raw-url` ?) which is exactly that same as the existing `@parcel/packager-raw` except for:
```diff
 import assert from 'assert';
 import {Packager} from '@parcel/plugin';
+import {replaceURLReferences} from '@parcel/utils';

 export default new Packager({
-  package({bundle}) {
+  async package({bundle, bundleGraph}) {
     let assets = [];
     bundle.traverseAssets(asset => {
       assets.push(asset);
     });

     assert.equal(assets.length, 1, 'Raw bundles must only contain one asset');
-    return {contents: assets[0].getStream()};
+    return {
+      contents: replaceURLReferences({
+        bundle,
+        bundleGraph,
+        contents: await assets[0].getCode(),
+        relative: false,
+      }).contents,
+    };
   },
 });
```

- All our tests are essentially integration tests, so you can simply merge your two tests into one.
- Please don't hardcode bundle hashes into the test (`'/image.ba250946.jpeg'`), that hash might not be stable, for example use a regex `image\.[a-f0-9]+\.jpeg`.
